/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - The film model imagines a stagnant layer of thickness δ next to the interface.
   - kc is the mass transfer coefficient (m/s); D is diffusivity (m²/s); δ is the equivalent film thickness (m).
   - Penetration theory treats contact as short and unsteady.
   - kc is the mass transfer coefficient (m/s); D is diffusivity (m²/s); t is exposure time (s); π is 3.1416.
   - Surface renewal theory removes the single exposure time.
   - kc is the mass transfer coefficient (m/s); D is diffusivity (m²/s); s is the fractional surface renewal rate (s⁻¹).
   - Measured exponents of D usually fall between 0.5 and 1.
*/
