/* book: lead: Momentum, heat and mass all cross the same thin fluid layer near a wall. In turbulent flow the same eddies carry all three. This shared motion lets one measured pressure drop predict a heat-transfer coefficient or a mass-transfer coefficient kc. Engineers use it when a correlation is missing or when a quick check is needed, for example to estimate evaporation from a straight smooth duct using the  */
